# Mock Gate tests
#
# The mock gate lets our own gate act as a remote peer (EU-MOCK) by registering
# a second gate row that points to the same eDelivery endpoint and certificate.
# When our gate sends an AS4 message to EU-MOCK it arrives at our own eDelivery,
# which processes it through the normal handler pipeline and returns the response.
#
# Prerequisites: own gate (EU-EE) must already exist in the database.

### [Auth] Login as admin
POST {{RUUTER_URL}}/auth/dev-login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "personalCode": "60001019906", "firstName": "Super", "lastName": "Admin" }

> {%
  client.test("[Auth] admin JWT issued", () => {
    client.assert(response.status === 200)
    client.global.set("adminToken", response.body.token)
  })
%}

### Setup — get own gate details
GET {{RUUTER_URL}}/efti/api/v1/gates/own
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

> {%
  client.test("Own gate exists", () => {
    client.assert(response.status === 200)
    client.assert(response.body.id === "EU-EE")
    client.global.set("ownGate", response.body)
  })
%}

### Setup — create mock gate (same eDelivery endpoint + cert as EU-EE, hardcoded:
# the cert contains newlines, and {{ownGate.eDeliveryCert}} interpolation would
# splice raw newlines into this JSON body and break it)
POST {{RUUTER_URL}}/admin/v1/gates
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

{
  "id": "EU-MOCK",
  "countryCode": "EE",
  "eDeliveryUrl": "http://edelivery:8081",
  "eDeliveryCert": "-----BEGIN CERTIFICATE-----\nMIIDATCCAemgAwIBAgIUB+wp45qwsgT0vhrdKm7e0LtM1SQwDQYJKoZIhvcNAQEL\nBQAwEDEOMAwGA1UEAwwFRVUtRUUwHhcNMjYwODI1MTQzMjE3WhcNMjcwODI1MTQz\nMjE3WjAQMQ4wDAYDVQQDDAVFVS1FRTCCASIwDQYJKoZIhvcNAQEBBQADggEPADCC\nAQoCggEBAKjlsmU2txVTCqvdJYhitJZ27Rd3DPHw/65puwMhRvFS+8SP5jaX3gpC\ne59EZzEab6IS7vK4bfHcL3Nc8986QnKm1kkse74Ou5X8k4EUf2cbeDNJJZ4TZ7Lk\nBTTPCsM5IR2BelmoLCoR+0PygefUwQVF1bZagfuQP/Q3gdQ/EuvqSHDEsceuNtIt\n3y20TKlCjQqNu4uuDpIYb3Jj99z0yoXwdU70/A//7Cz9Gb8WQVoMCrRsEI60k6yO\nqLrEXw2bw2hjYFrwCSCIvC2MHXKoZNvb5e35QZgdmC2e3JV4/85yZsBJhYlobFMR\niq17R0EWR0uJHQE5cmommxRjuAulKJ8CAwEAAaNTMFEwHQYDVR0OBBYEFHwdpyXY\nXQoqggPuCttLNLsDFXOXMB8GA1UdIwQYMBaAFHwdpyXYXQoqggPuCttLNLsDFXOX\nMA8GA1UdEwEB/wQFMAMBAf8wDQYJKoZIhvcNAQELBQADggEBAIACmHyOFBqoglic\n9kA99HRGzlRou6BIOBOjmscJOfaKZDsgp0gKhy1jdcobH+HvKWbMLE+gtOb+pFXC\nKafAfs3WssIiRU8eu/Vb1EbXR45kDW/OxL05H0StJsFspP7UtZSh5u+YrtQJw1T6\nJC/ZuARicSMrOtQpEGK3TcCMH8j+qJv6gLmzgf6RkFCQBM967GKo8LwArOyFFkhQ\nZXDJ5hI34jqON91kqmfXfCgx8eGGR3XxYz5pM5MluD0Zy2JOCGu2GLBvHoKvS/6C\n/8uXBeR2cXcgGLpv6KmEmGXDvzHTXDsbccHjvOi9JVi29J0Af9C0/Cy766UEFSOC\np2CFSAM=\n-----END CERTIFICATE-----\n",
  "status": "ONLINE"
}

> {%
  client.test("Mock gate created", () => {
    client.assert(response.status === 201)
    client.assert(response.body.id === "EU-MOCK")
    client.assert(response.body.status === "ONLINE")
  })
%}

### DISABLED — gate-to-gate loopback is blocked by two dev-side bugs:
#   1. edelivery ResqlClient.fetch crashes on a ReSQL error response instead of
#      failing gracefully (klite parses the {error} object as List -> no constructor)
#   2. GET /efti/get_platforms returns 400 'invalid byte sequence 0x00' once the
#      platform tests have run, so the ping-triggered party-registry reload fails.
# Re-enable once InternalRoutes.ping / the party registry survive a partial reload.

### Setup — reload eDelivery party registry (ping triggers reload)
# POST {{EDELIVERY_URL}}/api/v1/ping/EU-EE

